==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[ignore]] or [[disregard]]; to be [[indifferent]] to.
#: {{ux|en|He '''shrugged off''' the insults and proceeded despite them.}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=December 21, 2011
|author=Tom Rostance
|title=Fulham 0 - 5 Man Utd
|work=BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/16173202.stm
|page=
|passage=Manchester United '''shrugged off''' injuries to Phil Jones and Ashley Young to thrash a lifeless Fulham side.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=12 November 2021|author=Dan Shive|title=El Goonish Shive|section=Comic for Friday, Nov 12, 2021|sectionurl=https://www.egscomics.com/comic/balance-082|format=webcomic|text="I... don't understand."  "I assume he doesn't, either, and were you anyone else, he would '''shrug it off'''.  He, however, is your father.  His default response is protective concern, and he doesn't understand why you transform.  Lacking understanding, he is burdened by questions."}}

